  <CaseSection id="decision-review" title="A review step for misheard entries">
    <CaseProse>
      <p>
        Providers asked to capture by voice in the moment and review later. When the
        app can’t match an entry, it goes to review instead of guessing.
      </p>
      <p>
        A failed entry is saved with its words, translation, and recording, and
        whatever the app partly understood. Tapping the word that was the child’s
        name teaches the app that mishearing for good.
      </p>
      <p>
        Out loud, the app just says <em>&ldquo;processing unknown event for
        unrecognized child&rdquo;</em> instead of announcing a failure to a room of
        children.
      </p>
    </CaseProse>

